Z||000003||johnt671||08-29-2001||05:51 PM||||It's been running fine since spring.  I started the car up this morning to go to work and it started fine.  I pulled it out of the garage and got out to shut the garage door and as it reached the point when the idle speed drops to normal, the car died and won't restart.  Took the fuel line off before the fuel filter and fuel just trickled out instead of squirting out under pressure.  I had a problem in the spring because the car wouldn't start until the oil pressure lite went out and it turned out to be a computer problem so the computer was replaced.  AS covered in the first post, the car will start if I prime it, but then stalls out after the fuel runs out. There is no fuel spraying out of the injector when I try to start it.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||08-29-2001||09:33 PM||||You need to have oil pressure for the fuel pump to run.  Check fuel pump fuse, If the oil pressure idiot light goes out when you are cranking, you  have oil pressure, you should hear the fuel pump whirr.<P>Fuel filter plugged, bad fuel pump.||||reg||1
Z||000005||johnt671||08-30-2001||06:46 AM||||The fuse is good and the car won't start when the oil pressure lite goes out.  I did see s splice on the hot wire to the fuel pump so I'm going to check that out when I get the chance. I'm hopeing it's not the fuel pump cause I can't do that myself and I hate to send the car to the shop. Thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||08-30-2001||11:36 AM||||Are you getting a Check Engine light with the key "on" and engine off?  If not....<P>Does engine start?<BR>Your answer would be "No" <BR>1.Is ecm battery feed ckt 240 and ecm fuse ok?<BR>Now the battery feed ckt 240 is coming out of your ecm in two locations C16, and B1. Both of these wires are orange, and splice togather at the insterment panel connector. ECM fuse is the Pink/Black wire at A6 on the ecm. It is also called circuit 439. So now you have to answer the question "are they ok?"<BR>Yes- Ign. off, disconnect ecm, ign. on, probe ckt 240&439 with test light to ground. Is the light "on" on both circuits? Yes move on to set 2. No repair open in circuit the did not light the test light.<BR>No- Locate and correct short to ground in circuit that had a blown fuse. <BR>2.Faulty ECM grounds or ECM (which it shouldn't be the ECM itself, because you tried it in a different Fiero, and the problem did not move over to that Fiero) <BR>Hope this did something positive for you. <BR>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT<BR>3.2 Liter Under Construction<P>OK, lets do some steps.<BR>First off we need the service engine light to work.<BR>1) Check for a good ground at pin 'A' at the serial port. (ALCL Connector)<BR>2) Check the 'gauge' fuse in the fuse block.<BR>3) Make sure that both the fuel pump relay and the oil pressure switch and relay are connected and good. <BR>At the ECM connectors (not the ECM) <BR>4) Pin (row) C16 +12 volts (battery, from Fuse link)<BR>5) Pin (row) B1 +12 volts (for memory from Fuse link)<BR>6) Pin (row) A6 +12 volts (Switch ON! from Fuse block)<BR>7) Pin (row) A12 (ohms) to ground, 0 reading. <BR>Try from here, this is just for the Service Engine light!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||johnt671||08-31-2001||05:28 PM||||Found the problem.  The prior owner had a splice on the hot wire from the battery.  as I pulled the tape off the splice corrosion started falling out.  Cleaned and respliced and car started right up.  Now to soder in a good connection and weatherproof it.  By the way,  liquid electrical tape is highly flamable but don,t ask how I know.  Thanks for the advice.||||reg||1
